      "description": "Reference: WRF 4.8 em_scm_xy single-column run (GNU real32 build, dt = 60 s, 59 layers, mp = 6, sfclay = 1, slab, YSU) at call 120 (step 60, 20:00 UTC), replayed through the real64 kernels/wsm6_driver; WRF layers 20-59 mapped onto lev 1-40 (esm-spec 6.6 tests cannot rebind NLEV, and the only condensate, cloud ice qi <= 5e-5, sits in WRF layers 50-59). Ice-only regime with no precipitation: cloud-ice deposition is active in WRF layers 51-57 (lev 32-38, up to 3.3e-8 kg/kg/s, all unlimited), nucleation in WRF layers 54-55 (lev 35-36, 1.2e-9, LIMITED by the vapor budget: the unlimited adjustment rate is 1e4 times larger, so the applied pigen_lim is what is spot-checked); every snow/graupel process and the aggregations are exactly zero. Same tolerance reasoning as the supercell tests; residuals pidep 3.2e-8, pigen 1.8e-9 of column maximum.",
